endobj

484 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 81 0 R/T(Awhile loop isnatural when the number of validattempts is not fixed in advance: blank entries must be ignored, and \(see the changed condition\) the limit itself can change during the loop. A for loop with range\(3\) fixes the count at the start. If the counter is updated before the blank check, a blank entry consumes an attempt: the demo ['', '', '', '482913'] gave VERIFIED with the correct design but LOCKED with the misplaced counter, so a customer who pressed Enter three times was locked out before typing the OTP. Updating the counter after a successful break check \(or both before the loop test\) has the opposite risk of allowing extra attempts. )/E(Awhile loop isnatural when the number of validattempts is not fixed in advance: blank entries must be ignored, and \(see the changed condition\) the limit itself can change during the loop. A for loop with range\(3\) fixes the count at the start. If the counter is updated before the blank check, a blank entry consumes an attempt: the demo ['', '', '', '482913'] gave VERIFIED with the correct design but LOCKED with the misplaced counter, so a customer who pressed Enter three times was locked out before typing the OTP. Updating the counter after a successful break check \(or both before the loop test\) has the opposite risk of allowing extra attempts. )/Pg 16 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

