<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 85 0 R/T(join\(\)fastest,thenf-string/+=\(similar\),+= slowest as the number of lines grows. Strings are immutable, so text += p in principle creates a new string and copies all characters so far on every iteration: total characters copied about 1+2+...+n = O\(n2\). join\(\) first computes the total length, allocates once and copies each part once: O\(n\). The f-string builds each line efficiently but is still appended with +=, so it has the same growth as +=. )/E(join\(\)fastest,thenf-string/+=\(similar\),+= slowest as the number of lines grows. Strings are immutable, so text += p in principle creates a new string and copies all characters so far on every iteration: total characters copied about 1+2+...+n = O\(n2\). join\(\) first computes the total length, allocates once and copies each part once: O\(n\). The f-string builds each line efficiently but is still appended with +=, so it has the same growth as +=. )/Pg 20 0 R/K[2 4 3]>>
endobj

