999 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/P 90 0 R/T(Let ways\(n\) be the number of ways to climb n steps with moves of 1 or 2. The last move was either a 1-step from n-1 or a 2-step from n-2, so ways\(n\) = ways\(n-1\) + ways\(n-2\) \(recursive case\). Base case: ways\(0\) = ways\(1\) = 1 \(one way to stay at the bottom; one way to climb a single step\). The recursion always moves towards n <= 1, so it terminates. )/E(Let ways\(n\) be the number of ways to climb n steps with moves of 1 or 2. The last move was either a 1-step from n-1 or a 2-step from n-2, so ways\(n\) = ways\(n-1\) + ways\(n-2\) \(recursive case\). Base case: ways\(0\) = ways\(1\) = 1 \(one way to stay at the bottom; one way to climb a single step\). The recursion always moves towards n <= 1, so it terminates. )/Pg 25 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

