2413 0 obj
<</Title(Let ways\(n\) be the number of ways to climb n steps with moves of 1 or 2. The last move was either a 1-step from n-1 or a 2-step from n-2, so ways\(n\) = ways\(n-1\) + ways\(n-2\) \(recursive case\). Base case: ways\(0\) = ways\(1\) = 1 \(one way to stay at the bottom; one way to climb a single step\). The recursion always moves towards n <= 1, so it terminates.)/Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2403 0 R>>
endobj

2414 0 obj
<</Title(ways\(3\) is computed twice, ways\(2\) three times and ways\(1\) five times; only ways\(5\), ways\(4\) are computed once. 15 calls for n = 5, of which only 6 compute a new value. Memoisation stores each ways\(k\) the first time it is found)/Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2404 0 R>>
endobj

