2454 0 obj
<</Title(Options tested: \(A\) raising the limit to 5000 works \(209-digit answer\) but only moves the ceiling and risks a real stack overflow for very large n; \(B\) rewriting with a loop that keeps two values works for any n with O\(1\) space and is fastest \(0.000029 s against 0.000214 s for memo at n = 1000\); \(C\) filling the cache bottom-up \(calling ways_memo\(100\), \(200\)...\) keeps recursion shallow. Decision: use the loop \(B\) for deployment, up to 1,000 steps and beyond, because it has no depth limit, no cache memory and the simplest failure behaviour. I would not raise the limit as the only fix. I would keep the memoised recursive version only as the readable, tested reference implementation to verify the loop against \(they agree: True\), and raise the limit only if recursion must be kept, together with the memo.)/Dest[30 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2446 0 R/Prev 2467 0 R>>
endobj

